        "tenancy": "EXERCISED via scripts/toolloop/regwf_tenancy_probe.py, which seeds the population the registry was missing: it held ZERO tier='user' rows, so the claim had nothing to bite on. Two throwaway rows, both torn down and re-counted clean: one owned by the caller (019d5e3c…), one by a stranger (01900000-…-dead). RESULT: count 13, the caller's own row RETURNED, the stranger's row NOT returned. Both arms are required — a negative-only check passes just as well when a tool ignores user-tier rows altogether, which would be a different bug wearing a green tick."
