          "test_file": "services/chat-service/tests/test_the_plain_speech_guard_does_not_invent_workflow_names.py",
          "invariant": "THE §4 GUARD TRANSLATES A WORD; IT MAY NEVER HALF-TRANSLATE A NAME. Rewriting part of a hyphenated identifier does not produce plainer English, it produces an identifier that does not exist — 'story bible-bootstrap' for glossary-bootstrap. Translating a WHOLE name is a different act and stays legal: the vision-to-book rule matches its entire token and still yields 'book-building'.",
          "red_on_original": "PROVEN RED. With the guard reverted in place (and restored by explicit write, verified by sha256 — never `git checkout`, which would discard whatever else is uncommitted in the file): 2 failed, 3 passed. The failure is the defect in its own words — \"the guard rewrote the identifier 'glossary-bootstrap' into 'story bible-bootstrap', which is not a workflow that exists\". The 3 that stayed green are the ones asserting the guard still translates prose, so the file cannot be satisfied by neutering it.",
          "past_incidents_checked": "SWEPT the identifier populations, not just the one that surfaced it. Underscored names were never in the class at all — `_` is a regex word character, so \\bglossary\\b never matched inside glossary_propose_entities or composition_glossary_build (0 of 30 workflow step tool names rewritten, before or after).\n\n    population                 old guard rewrote   new guard rewrites\n    workflow slugs (12)               3                   1\n    skill slugs (27)                  6                   6\n    step tool names (30)              0                   0\n\n🔴 AND THE SWEEP FOUND A RESIDUAL MY FIX DOES NOT COVER, which is why it was worth running. The 1 remaining workflow slug is vision-to-book, whose rewrite is deliberate and whole-token. The 6 skill slugs are all the literal slug `glossary` (1 system + 5 user-tier), which the guard still renders as 'story bible'. A hyphen guard cannot help a bare identifier that IS a jargon word, so the class is genuinely wider than the invariant above.\n\nWhether those 6 are a BUG is the same question as vision-to-book and is not mine to settle: rendering the skill as 'story bible' is arguably the intended relabel, and only becomes a defect where the reader must type the name back. It is recorded rather than quietly counted as covered — this fix closes the measured 5/5 invented-name defect, not the whole class."
